{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Shoham stones.</b> Two were needed there for the ephod's requirement, as stated in ״וְאַתָּה תְּצַוֶּה״ (Exodus 28)." "<b>Setting.</b> So called because they make for them a gold setting like a גֻּמָּא, and place the stone there to fill the גֻּמָּא — therefore they are called stones of setting (אַבְנֵי מִלּוּאִים), and the place of the setting is called מִשְׁבֶּצֶת." "<b>For the ephod and for the breastpiece.</b> The shoham stones for the ephod and the setting stones for the breastpiece; and breastpiece and ephod are specified in ״וְאַתָּה תְּצַוֶּה״ (Exodus 28), and they are kinds of ornament."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "גֻּמָּא: a hollow socket or cell; the word is left transliterated as Rashi uses the technical term."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:23.805446671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}